  WHAT THIS REPORT EVIDENCES
    The class extends EasyMockSupport, so all twelve tests exercise the mocking
    library whose version advances from 4.1 to 5.6.0 - the widest-footprint
    test-library change in the migration. Both 4.1 and the intermediate 4.3
    fail identically on Java 17 with an inaccessible-object error raised from
    the library's class proxy factory, because a core platform package is not
    opened to the unnamed module; 5.6.0 succeeds. The resolution was to UPGRADE
    THE LIBRARY, never to relax the JDK module boundaries. That library is used
    by seven of this module's eight unit-test classes.
    Behaviourally the twelve tests cover complaint event handling: assignee
    change, participant added and deleted, priority change, location update
    including the previously-empty case, status change, calendar-folder
    deletion, and details change including the previously-null case, plus two
    guard cases for a null event and a non-complaint source.
    This module declares no removed-mocking-framework dependency and no
    class-extension dependency, so it is correctly absent from the twelve-POM
    and five-POM removal lists; only the root aggregator mocking-library
    version property reaches it, and the module POM itself is untouched.
    The class carries no runner annotation, so it runs as plain JUnit 4.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS FOLDER
    The module also declares six integration-test classes. They produce no
    report here, because a unit-test run stops at the test phase while the
    integration-test runner's goals are declared with no explicit phase and so
